'''''Rosa abietina''''' is a species of [[rose]] that was described by [[Jean Charles Marie Grenier]]. ''Rosa abietina'' is part of the genus ''[[Rosa (plant)|Rosa]]''<ref name="PoWO"/><ref name="source">{{Cite web |url=http://worldplants.webarchiv.kit.edu/ |title=World Plants: Synonymic Checklists of the Vascular Plants of the World |access-date=2022-09-19 |archive-date=2019-03-18 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190318221109/http://worldplants.webarchiv.kit.edu/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |last=Grénier |first=Charles |url=https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k6580517m/f243.item |title=Flore de la chaîne jurassique |date=1865 |language=FR}}</ref> and is an insect flower from the family [[Rosaceae]]. 

